        <article class="article-card">
          <h2 class="card-title">
            <a href="/articles/strange-signals-called-long-period-radio-transits-come-from-cataclysmic-variables">Strange Signals Called Long-period Radio Transits Come From Cataclysmic Variables</a>
          </h2>

          <div class="card-meta">
            <span>
              By <a href="/authors/ion23drive.html">Evan Gough</a> - August 21, 2026 07:59 PM UTC | <a href="/categories/stars.html">Stars</a>
            </span>
          </div>

          <a href="/articles/strange-signals-called-long-period-radio-transits-come-from-cataclysmic-variables">
            
              <img src="/article_images/ASKAP-Rose-WD-e1780465074367_20260820_225651.jpg" alt="" class="featured-image">
            
          </a>

          <div class="card-excerpt">
            
              Long-period Radio Transients are sources that emit repeating radio and x-ray signals. The signals are polarized and coherent, and are similar to pulsars in some respects. But the type of astrophysical object responsible for them has been vigorously debated. New research says that at least one of them comes from a cataclysmic variable, a binary star where a white dwarf and a red dwarf orbit closely.
            
          </div>

          <a href="/articles/strange-signals-called-long-period-radio-transits-come-from-cataclysmic-variables" class="read-more">Continue reading</a>
        </article>
      
